+| R19 | 100-102 | Integer `I1 % I2` becomes K `I1 modInt I2`, guarded by nonzero `I2` | Trusted primitive bridge; `<k>` only. | On the actual nonnegative operands and positive divisors, K modulo equals Python modulo. |
